# fleet-launch allowlist — stage a copy per Mac (your config manager is the natural place), then install
# it root-owned with:   install-fleet-launch.sh --list
#
# One command per line: its EXACT argument list, the program first, arguments separated by a TAB — not
# spaces. fleet-launch runs a command only if that whole line matches. Lines starting with # are ignored.
# Use absolute paths, and list only scripts and programs you would trust with this Mac's approvals.
#
# Examples (replace <you>, and use real TABs between arguments):
/Users/<you>/.local/bin/fleet-local-check
/Users/<you>/.local/bin/<your-sync-script>.sh
